 These substitutes are not Opus models, so the `medium` rule for a value that resolves to an Opus model does not apply to them on Codex. On Codex the level listed above for each substitute takes the place of the sheet's `default effort` line; a level the role value names with `@` still applies.
 
+When `gpt-6.2-sol` cannot run (no Codex quota or Codex unavailable), fall back to `gemini-4-neon-xhigh`: for unattended coding, run `agy-yolo` (`agy --dangerously-skip-permissions --sandbox --settings` with `agentMode: ""`, `allowNonWorkspaceAccess: false`, `enableTerminalSandbox: true`, and `permissions.deny: ["unsandboxed(*)"]`) inside a dedicated worktree **strictly within an enclosing external container/VM sandbox** (which bounds files, credentials, lifecycle hooks, plugins, and workspace MCP servers) when unattended execution is explicitly authorized; without an enclosing container/VM, do not run unattended auto-approved coding commands (run interactively with per-action approval in Default sandboxed mode or report blocked). For read-only review, prefer `autoreview --engine agy --model gemini-4-neon-xhigh`, or plain `agy` (never `--dangerously-skip-permissions`) from a clean empty temporary directory verified outside any Git checkout with an isolated auth-only `HOME` and `USERPROFILE`, Default-mode strict deny-all `--settings`, stdin `stream-json`, and `--sandbox`. Never use this fallback in repositories declaring client, personal, or regulated data, or where the owner has not approved that provider; host-policy or task restrictions are not a reason to route around them. Record the substitution and why `gpt-6.2-sol` could not run.
+
 `/setup-pstack` writes the configured model list. On Codex, set it to your Codex model slugs.
 
